(meta (title "Markdown, where it is quicker")
      (date 2026-09-26))

Some things are quicker to write in Markdown, and samizdat reads it, into the
same tree as the rest of the page:

@markdown|{
A *list* of things, with a [link](menus.html):

- [x] tables and task lists,
- [ ] and footnotes,[^1] numbered with the page's own.

[^1]: Like this one.
}|

A whole file of Markdown can be included too. The section below is
@code{_imported.md}, beside this note. Its name begins with @code{_}: a
@code{.md} that is not hidden would be in the menu as well, and served as it
is.

@include-markdown["_imported.md"]

